     "text": "{\"count\": 2, \"rationale\": \"Block tokenCache:credentialAccess and backupHost:lateralMovement. Blocking tokenCache disables apiToken, dbLogin and rdpLogin. That makes printServer unreachable, which kills shareMount and secretsManager. It also makes jumpHost and hypervisor unreachable, which kills dbReplica. Blocking backupHost then kills codeRepo and serviceAccount, which also cuts vaultRead. All four parents of crownData:exfiltrate are now unreachable. One block cannot work: codeRepo is reachable through backupHost, which kerberoast reaches straight from the footholds. shareMount is reachable through printServer, which has an independent tokenCache/dbLogin/rdpLogin path. So no single step cuts both.\"}"
    }
